dynrec: add MIPS64 backend

MIPS64 (MIPS IV and later, n64 ABI, big-endian) backend derived from the
Alpha and sparc64 ones, using the generic hooks. 32bit values are kept
sign-extended in registers as the ABI requires. Helpers are called with
$25 loaded from a call target pool, with a direct jal as the code cache is
placed in the 256MB jal region of the executable; parameter loads fill the
delay slots. Memory and stack accesses look up the TLB inline, branch
conditions and the carry into ADC/SBB/RCL/RCR are evaluated inline.

Flag-setting ALU operations, shifts and INC/DEC, FPU arithmetic, stack and
loads/stores are inline, block links are patched to j, aligned dword reads
use one lw with a register byte swap. Uses the generic hooks; the 3DBENCH
steps from string operations on include the generic changes.

Performance on an SGI O2 (R12000 400 MHz), DOSBox cycles=max,
machine=svga_s3, SB Pro, measured under Xvfb:

  Test                    normal core   dynamic core   speedup
  3DBENCH                  4.6 fps      14.9 fps       3.24x
  Doom -timedemo demo3                   7.9 fps
                                        (9511 rt, 2134 gametics)
  Quake +timedemo demo1                  1.9 fps
                                        (497.8 s, 969 frames)

  3DBENCH steps (dynamic core, single runs, about +-1 fps variation)
  initial backend                         9.6 fps
  inline TLB memory accesses             10.5 fps
  inline branch conditions               11.1 fps
  delay slot filling                     11.2 fps
  call target pool and direct jal        11.3 fps
  string operations on page runs         11.7 fps
  inline push/pop, carry, indirect link  11.9 fps
  block writes into chained VGA memory   14.2 fps
  link patching, inline flag operations  14.4 fps
  inline FPU, byte swapped dword reads   14.9 fps

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

